## Third-party components and references

OpenMesh is an independent implementation. It contains no code from the projects below; they
were studied as prior art and for hardware pin-map facts, and are credited here.

- Reticulum / LXMF / LXST — Mark Qvist (https://reticulum.network/). LXST and its Rust port
  rsLXST are under a restrictive licence and are NOT used.
- Ratspeak and rsReticulum/rsLXMF — https://ratspeak.org/ (Reticulum Licence). Their Rust
  architecture informed OpenMesh's client/daemon split.
- Meshtastic firmware (GPL-3.0) — board pin maps and variant files were consulted to cross-check
  hardware wiring for the reference boards; OpenMesh board headers are written independently and
  cite the vendor documentation.
  The PlatformIO board definitions in `firmware/boards/pio/*.json` and the nRF52 Arduino board
  variants in `firmware/variants/*/` are derived from meshtastic/firmware (GPL-3.0). They are
  included here under GPL-3.0 terms, which AGPL-3.0 permits (GPLv3 §13 / AGPLv3 §13); they are
  configuration files only and contain no Meshtastic application logic. If this distinction
  matters to you, the files are isolated under those two directories.
- MeshCore (https://meshcore.io/) — protocol design inspiration (repeater/room-server roles).
- Semtech AN1200.13/AN1200.22 — LoRa airtime formulas.

## Bundled Rust dependencies with copyleft terms

### `codec2` crate 0.3.1 — pure-Rust Codec2 implementation

- Licence: **LGPL-2.1-only AND MIT** (see the crate's `Cargo.toml`; Codec2 itself is by David Rowe
  and contributors, LGPL-2.1).
- Upstream: <https://github.com/scriptjunkie/codec2> (pure-Rust port used through
  <https://crates.io/crates/codec2>).
- Linked statically into `openmesh-voice`, `openmesh-voice-wasm` and `openmesh-ffi` (host, WASM and
  Android builds). It is used unmodified.
- The OpenMesh project as a whole is AGPL-3.0-or-later and publishes its complete corresponding
  source; that source distribution covers the LGPL source/relinking obligations for this
  dependency. If you redistribute binaries, keep the LGPL notice and the offer/means to relink
  against a modified Codec2; no Codec2 source files are modified here.

### Bundled AVIF encoder — `ravif` / `rav1e`

- `ravif` 0.13 (crates.io, <https://github.com/kornelski/cavif-rs>) — **BSD-3-Clause**.
- `rav1e` 0.8 / `v_frame` / `av1-grain` (crates.io, <https://github.com/xiph/rav1e/>) —
  **BSD-2-Clause**.
- `avif-serialize` 0.8 — **BSD-3-Clause**; `rgb` — **MIT**; remaining transitive crates are
  MIT/Apache-2.0/Zlib/CC0 permutations.
- Linked statically into `openmesh-image`, `openmesh-image-wasm` and `openmesh-ffi` (host, WASM
  and Android builds) to provide AVIF encoding when platform encoders are unavailable. No files
  are modified.
- **AV1 patent policy:** AV1 is covered by the AOMedia royalty-free patent policy
  (<https://aomedia.org/license/patent-license/>); this is noted for downstream distributors and
  is not legal advice.

